  "live_records": {
    "q-36521": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36521",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}=(x{y}^{2}+2y){e}^{xy}+2{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}=6x{z}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate the following expression at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nHence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x} & =\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x{y}^{2}+2y){e}^{xy}+2{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =(x{y}^{2}+2y)\\cdot x{e}^{xy}+(2xy+2)\\cdot {e}^{xy}+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4xy+2){e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn addition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6x{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =12xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate both partial derivatives at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =(0+0+2){e}^{0}=2 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =12(1)(1)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,0,1)}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =2+12=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
